#ROOMS

#53750
"Main Room"
"This long corridor with its clean walls and hardwood flooring, is light and

airy, the sunlight seems to float between these walls.  The ceiling runs about

twenty feet tall, topped with an elaborate pendentive dome where four vaults

from the north, south, east, and west meet.  Paintings of three elves hang

over the northern, western, and eastern doors.  An opening to the east leads

to the practice rooms, while the west narrows into a small foyer.  Massive

steel bound oak doors at the end of this hall seem to be the only entrance or

exit from this lodging.

"
""
