#53756
"Mountains"
"The air is thin, with an occasionally cool breeze from the north brushing

against your cheeks.  Impeding progress eastward is a rock wall that reaches

an unsurmountable height.  Several little pieces of gravel have collected at

the base of the wall from those who have attempted to climb it.  Westward, the

ground becomes paved and is no longer as rocky.

"
